                <pb facs="0607" n="601" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg601"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Newport, R.
                                I.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1893-09-18"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 18,
                    1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Gresham</hi>: I gather from a telegram which
                    I have received from the Earl of Rosebery, that the prolonged absence of the, U.
                    S. land commissioner from Samoa is causing inconvenience, and I should be glad
                    if you would enable me to inform his lordship at what date that gentleman may be
                    expected to return to his post.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
